# Edges 0, 2 and 4 lie on the three lines y=0, x=0 and y=x, so all three
# project through the origin. Their heights there are 0, 1 and 2, so the
# triple point is resolvable but only by the perturbation.
note = three pairwise non-adjacent segments concurrent at one projected point
knot = unknot
multiple_points      == 1
max_point_multiplicity == 3
transversal          >= 3
spatial              == 0

# KNOWN CRASH (2026-08-13), LinkEmbedding only. RequireIntersections segfaults
# when three segments project through one common point. Bisected on this
# fixture: moving any one of the three concurrent edges off the origin makes it
# complete normally, and widening the z-separation does not help, so the trigger
# is the concurrency itself and not a near-tie in depth. LinkEmbedding2/3/4
# resolve it correctly (6 crossings, matching the explicit shear). Under
# --isolate this is scored; otherwise it is skipped to keep the run alive.
xcrash_invariant = 1 | segfault in LinkEmbedding::RequireIntersections on a triple point
